WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.727
Production RAG also introduces security and trust concerns.

00:00:04.727 --> 00:00:12.072
First, access control. A user should never receive a chunk they are not authorized to see.

00:00:12.072 --> 00:00:19.162
Permission filters should be applied during retrieval, not after sensitive text has already entered the prompt.

00:00:19.162 --> 00:00:22.712
Second, retrieved documents are untrusted data.

00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:28.952
A document might contain text that looks like an instruction to the language model.

00:00:28.952 --> 00:00:34.914
The system should treat that content as source material, not as a trusted system command.

00:00:35.696 --> 00:00:37.948
Third, show sources.

00:00:37.948 --> 00:00:45.768
Returning titles, source paths, chunk IDs, and sometimes retrieval scores helps users and developers verify the

00:00:45.768 --> 00:00:50.818
evidence. These are not optional cosmetic features.

00:00:50.818 --> 00:00:59.298
RAG connects language models to organizational data, so the retrieval layer becomes part of the security boundary.

00:00:59.298 --> 00:01:04.715
Good metadata and careful access design matter as much as embedding quality.
